From 7a37c05b0110bbf405f83c66258cefcb9419c529 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Szewczyk <a.szewczyk@cthings.co>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:47:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] scripts: sbom: do not put the local toolchain path in
 PackageDownloadLocation

Cherry-pick of one hunk from upstream nrfconnect/sdk-nrf#31393 ("scripts: sbom:
Update report to SPDX 2.3"), which is still a draft backport against
v3.4-branch. Only the toolchain hunk is taken here; the rest of that series
reshapes the SPDX output in ways this branch does not need.

register_toolchain_for_build() set the toolchain package's url to the resolved
install directory, and the SPDX template emits that as

    PackageDownloadLocation: /opt/toolchains/zephyr-sdk-0.17.4

A local filesystem path is not a download location - it tells a consumer
nothing and publishes where the build machine keeps its toolchain. With url
unset the template emits NONE, which is what SPDX expects when there is no
download location to give.

output_pre_process() skips a package whose url is None before it would
dereference it, and the toolchain package already sets package.name, so the
h2 heading in the HTML report - "name if name else url" - still names it. The
URL paragraph below that heading prints package.url unguarded and would render
the literal "None"; the next patch guards it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5 / Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Adam Szewczyk <a.szewczyk@cthings.co>
Upstream-Status: Partial backport [https://github.com/nrfconnect/sdk-nrf/commit/ad6eefca5fdd1cde673efc23077d1ce010be083d]
---
 scripts/west_commands/sbom/input_build.py | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/west_commands/sbom/input_build.py b/scripts/west_commands/sbom/input_build.py
index b162a17eb2..6b2b2e1baf 100644
--- a/scripts/west_commands/sbom/input_build.py
+++ b/scripts/west_commands/sbom/input_build.py
@@ -267,7 +267,6 @@ def register_toolchain_for_build(data: Data, build_dir: Path):
     pkg_version = version or detect_toolchain_version(resolved) or 'UNKNOWN'
     package.id = f'TOOLCHAIN#{pkg_name.upper()}#{pkg_version.upper()}'
     package.name = pkg_name
-    package.url = str(resolved)
     package.version = pkg_version
     package.root_path = resolved
     if args.package_supplier:
-- 
